          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            See
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            There are many
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structures on the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaf"} simplicial presheaves
            derived from the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
          %p
            The
            %em local
            such model structures are of interest in that they model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-stack+homotopically"} infinity-stacks
            so that they are a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presentation
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category+of+%28infinity%2C1%29-sheaves"} (infinity,1)-category of (infinity,1)-sheaves
            on the given
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
          %p They can be thought of as being obtained from global model structures, of which there are two:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+model+structure+on+simplicial+sheaves"} global projective
                model structure has weak equivalences and fibrations being
                %em objectwise
                those of
                = succeed "s;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            %li
              %p
                the
                %strong
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+model+structure+on+simplicial+sheaves"} global injective
                model structure has weak equivalences and cofibrations being
                %em objectwise
                those of
                = succeed "s;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
          %p
            These two model structures are Quillen equivalent (
            %em DHI04
            %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/K-theory/0563/spre.pdf#page=5"} p. 5
            with the Quillen equivalence given by the identity functor). They can be defined on any domain category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            then there is a notion of
            %em local weak equivalences
            of simplicial presheaves on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %em local
            projective and
            %em local
            injective model structures by applying left
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization"} Bousfield localization
            of the above model structures at local weak equivalences (see
            %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/PS_cache/math/pdf/0205/0205027v2.pdf#page=6"} p. 6
            of
            = succeed ")" do
              %em DHI04
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %strong local projective
                model structure (weak equivalences are locally (usually stalkwise) and cofibrations are those that have the left
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lifting+property"} lifting property
                against objectwise acyclic fibrations);
            %li
              %p
                the
                %strong local injective
                (weak equivalences are locally (usually stalkwise) and fibrations are those that have the right
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lifting+property"} lifting property
                against the objectwise acyclic cofibrations).
          %p
            %strong Warning
            Since the (homotopy classes) of weak equivalences do not form a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+set"} small set
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization+of+model+categories"} Bousfield localization of model categories
            does not apply. The existence of the Bousfield localization has to be shown by hand. For the injective structure this is what Joyal and Jardine accomplished.
          %p
            Again, the injective and projective local model structures are Quillen equivalent by the identity functors between the underlying categories and hence provide projective and injective versions of the corresponding homotopy theory of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-stack+homotopically"} infinity-stacks
          %p
            In the local injective structure all objects are cofibrant, so that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+category"} opposite category
            of simplicial presheaves with the local injective model structure is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} category of fibrant objects
          %p
            Both local model structures are proper
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} simplicially enriched
            categories (
            %em DHI04
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/K-theory/0563/spre.pdf#page=6"} p. 5
          %p
            The
            %em local injective
            model structure on simplicial presheaves is originally due to Jardine, following the construction of the Quillen equivalent local
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sheaves"} model structure on simplicial sheaves
            by Joyal. It was only later realized in
            %em DHI04
            as a left
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization"} Bousfield localization
            of the global injective model structure.
          %p In between the injective and the projective model structures there are many other model structures obtained by varying the class of generating global cofibrations.
          %p
            In the following let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            be a small
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            and denote by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SimpPr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SimpPr(S)
            be the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaf"} simplicial presheaves
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %h2#local_model_structures Local model structures
          %p
            One usually says that a
            %strong local model structure
            on a category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaves
            is one whose weak equivalences are not defined objectwise but on
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cover"} cover
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
          %h3#local_weak_equivalences Local weak equivalences
          %p
            There are different equivalent ways to define local weak equivalences of simplicial presheaves on a site
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
          %h3#in_terms_of_sheaves_of_homotopy_groups In terms of sheaves of homotopy groups
          %p
            (see section 2 of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Jardine07"} Jardine 2007
          %p We want to say that a local weak equivalence of simplicial presheaves is one which is “over each point” an isomorphism of homotopy groups.
          %p we need the following terminology about sheaves of simplicial homtopy groups:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0(X)
                for its set of connected components and
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n(X,x)
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 1
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ∈
                        %msub
                          %mi X
                          %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X_0
                = succeed "th" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                (the homotopy group of its
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi X
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mo ,
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n(X,x) = \pi_n(|X|, x)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                      %mo :
                      %mi SimpSet
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0 : SimpSet \to Set
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mi n
                        %mo :
                        %mi SimpSet
                        %mo →
                        %mi Grps
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n : SimpSet \to Grps
            %li
              %p
                By postcomposition these functors induce functors
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi π
                        %mn 0
                      %mo :
                      %msup
                        %mi SimpSet
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mi op
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi Set
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\pi_0 : SimpSet^{S^{op}} \to Set^{S^{op}}
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi π
                          %mi n
                        %mo :
                        %msup
                          %mi SimpSet
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mi op
                        %mo →
                        %msup
                          %mi Grps
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mi op
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\pi_n : SimpSet^{S^{op}} \to Grps^{S^{op}}
            %li
              %p
                By postcomposition with the sheafification functor this yields functors
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi π
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                        %mn 0
                      %mo :
                      %msup
                        %mi SimpSet
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi S
                            %mi op
                      %mo →
                      %mi Sh
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi S
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\tilde \pi_0 : SimpSet^{S^{op}} \to Sh(S)
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mover
                            %mi π
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mi n
                        %mo :
                        %msup
                          %mi SimpSet
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mi op
                        %mo →
                        %mi Sh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Grps
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\tilde \pi_n : SimpSet^{S^{op}} \to Sh(S,Grps)
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong local weak equivalence
              of simplicial presheaves is a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
              such that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mover
                            %mi π
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %msub
                          %mover
                            %mi π
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mn 0
                        %mi X
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mover
                            %mi π
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mn 0
                        %mi Y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde \pi_0(f) : \tilde \pi_0 X \to \tilde \pi_0 Y
                  is an isomorphism in
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Sh
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi S
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(S)
              %li
                %p the diagrams
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mrow
                          %mtable
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mover
                                    %mi π
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                                  %mi n
                                %mi X
                              %mtd
                                %mo →
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mover
                                    %mi π
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                                  %mi n
                                %mi Y
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mtd
                              %mtd
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mtr
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mover
                                    %mi X
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                                  %mn 0
                              %mtd
                                %mo →
                              %mtd
                                %msub
                                  %mover
                                    %mi Y
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                                  %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\array{
                        \\tilde \pi_n X &amp;\to&amp; \tilde \pi_n Y
                        \\\
                        \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                        \\\
                        \\tilde X_0
                        \&amp;\to&amp;
                        \\tilde Y_0
                        }
                %p
                  are pullback diagrams in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Sh
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi S
                          %mo ,
                          %mi SimpSet
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Sh(S,SimpSet)
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo ≥
                          %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 1
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mover
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                          %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde X_0
                  denotes the sheaf associated to
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi X
                            %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0
          %p
            Equivalently a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
            of simplicial presheaves is, equivalently, a local weak equivalence if all induced morphisms of sheaves
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi π
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi U
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mover
                      %mi π
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                    %mi n
                  %mi Y
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi U
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\tilde \pi_n (X|_U, x) \to \tilde \pi_n Y|_U, f(x)
          %p
            are isomorphisms for all
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in S
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi U
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X|_U, Y|_U
            the pullbacks to the over-category site
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S/U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X_0(U)
            and all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 0
          %p
            If the site
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            %em has enough points
            then this condition is equivalent to saying that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is a weak equivalence in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
            over every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stalk"} stalk
            (see
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Jardine01"} Jardine 2001 p. 363
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Jardine15"} Jardine 2015 pp. 63
          %h3#in_terms_of_local_liftings In terms of local liftings
          %p
            (see
            = succeed "," do
              %em DI02
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            are local fibrations there is a characterisation in terms of local homotopy liftings. Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            for the pushout of the diagram
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ←
                    %mo ∂
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial \Delta^n \leftarrow \partial \Delta^n\times \Delta^1 \rightarrow \Delta^n\times \Delta^1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^n\rightarrow P
            by restriction of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^n\times \Delta^1\rightarrow P
            along the cofaces.
          %p
            Then a local weak equivalence is a morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
            such that for all commuting diagrams
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo ∂
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mi n
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi U
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi i
                                %mi U
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi f
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mi n
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi U
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\partial \Delta^n \otimes U &amp;\to&amp; X
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow^{i_U} &amp;&amp; \downarrow^f
                  \\\
                  \\Delta^n \otimes U &amp;\to&amp; Y
                  }
          %p
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            simplicially constantly representable there exists a covering sieve
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            such that for every
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V\in R
            there are morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g:\Delta^n \otimes V\rightarrow X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo :
                  %mi P
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h:P\otimes V\rightarrow Y
            for which
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo ∘
                  %msub
                    %mi i
                    %mi V
                  %mo =
                  %mo ∂
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mo ∂
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi U
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g\circ i_V=\partial\Delta^n \otimes V\rightarrow \partial\Delta^n \otimes U \rightarrow X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi U
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^n\otimes V \rightarrow \Delta^n \otimes U\rightarrow Y= \Delta^n\otimes V\rightarrow P\otimes V\rightarrow Y
            and in addition the square
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi Δ
                            %mi n
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi V
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi f
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi P
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi U
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\Delta^n\otimes V &amp;\to&amp; X
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^f
                  \\\
                  P \otimes U &amp;\to&amp; Y
                  }
          %p commutes.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li Every object-wise weak equivalence is in particular a local weak equivalence.
          %h2#local_injective_model_structure Local injective model structure
          %p
            The
            %strong local injective model structure
            on simplicial presheaves on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is the
            %strong left
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization"} Bousfield localization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SPr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi loc
                      %mi inj
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SPr(C)_{loc inj}
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} injective global model structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SPr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi inj
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SPr(C)_{inj}
            at the class of local weak equivalences described above.
          %p So
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                cofibrations are precisely the objectwise cofibrations of simplicial sets, i.e. the monomorphisms in
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi SPr
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SPr(S)
            %li
              %p
                weak equivalences are the
                %em local weak equivalences
                from above.
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              The inclusion of sheaves into simplicial presheaves
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SimpSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi SimpPr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SimpSh(S) \hookrightarrow SimpPr(S)
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheafification"} sheafification
              functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SimpPr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi SimpSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SimpPr(S) \to SimpSh(S)
              constitute a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
              with respect to the above
              %em local injective model structure
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SimpPr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SimpPr(S)
              and the local
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sheaves"} model structure on simplicial sheaves
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Jardine07"}> Jardine 2007, Thm. 5
            )
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              The fibrant objects in the local injective model structure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SPr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi loc
                        %mi inj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SPr(C)_{loc inj}
              are those simplicial presheaves that
            %ol
              %li
                %p are fibrant in the global injective model structure;
              %li
                %p
                  satisfy
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
                  for all
                  = succeed "s." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercover"} hypercover
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              %em> DHI04
              , theorem 1.1
          %h2#local_projective_model_structure Local projective model structure
          %p
            The
            %strong local projective model structure
            on simplicial presheaves on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is the
            %strong left
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bousfield+localization"} Bousfield localization
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SPr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi loc
                      %mi proj
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SPr(C)_{loc proj}
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} projective global model structure
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SPr
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi proj
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SPr(C)_{proj}
            at the class of local weak equivalences described above.
          %p So
          %ul
            %li
              %p cofibrations are precisely the cofibrations in the global projective structure (defined by left lifting property with respect to global Kan fibrations)
            %li
              %p
                weak equivalences are the
                %em local weak equivalences
                from above.
          %p
            %strong> Remark
            \. Notice that this is still using
            %strong left
            Bousfield localization. If we used right Bousfield localization the local projective fibrations would simply be the global Kan fibrations. Instead we have the following.
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem_3 Theorem
            %p
              The local injective model structure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SPr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi loc
                        %mi inj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SPr(C)_{loc inj}
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalent
              to the “universal homotopy theory”
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U C/S
              constructed by
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  formally adding
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limit"} homotopy colimits
                  to the category
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                  to create the category
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi U
                          %mi C
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U C
              %li
                %p
                  imposing relations requiring that for every
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercover"} hypercover
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi U
                          %mo →
                          %mi X
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \to X
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi hocolim
                          %mi n
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi n
                        %mo →
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} hocolim_n U_n \to X
                  is a weak equivalence.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              %em> DHI04
              , theorem 1.2
          %p
            In
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U C/S
            the fibrant objects have a simpler description than in
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SPr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi loc
                        %mi inj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SPr(C)_{loc inj}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
            but the implicit fibrancy condition with respect to the global injective structure is replaced by the fibrancy condition with respect to the global projective structure
          .un_theorem
            %h6#theorem_4 Theorem
            %p
              The fibrant objects in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U C/S
              are those simplicial presheaves
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  are objectwise fibrant (i.e. take values in
                  = succeed "es)" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
              %li
                %p
                  satisfy
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
                  for all
                  = succeed "s." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercover"} hypercover
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              %em> DHI04
              , theorem 1.3
          %h2#intermediate_model_structures Intermediate model structures
          %p
            One can regard the projective and the injective model structure as two extrema of a poset of model structures on simplicial presheaves; see
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intermediate+model+structure"} intermediate model structure
          %h2#references References
          %p Eg.
          %ul
            %li#JardineLecture
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+F.+Jardine"}> John F. Jardine
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Simplicial presheaves
                %strong 47
                (1987) 35-87 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-4049(87)90100-9"}> doi:10.1016/0022-4049(87)90100-9
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://math.uchicago.edu/~amathew/simplicialpresheaves.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Jardine01
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+F.+Jardine"}> J. F. Jardine
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Stacks and the homotopy theory of simplicial sheaves
                %strong 3
                2 (2001) 361–384 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://dx.doi.org/10.4310/HHA.2001.v3.n2.a5"}> doi:10.4310/HHA.2001.v3.n2.a5
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://projecteuclid.org/journals/homology-homotopy-and-applications/volume-3/issue-2/Stacks-and-the-homotopy-theory-of-simplicial-sheaves/hha/1139840259.full"} euclid
            %li#Jardine07
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+F.+Jardine"}> John F. Jardine
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Simplicial Presheaves
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.uwo.ca/math/faculty/jardine/courses/fields/fields-01.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.uwo.ca/math/faculty/jardine/courses/fields/fields_lectures.html"} webpage
            %li#Jardine15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+F.+Jardine"}> John F. Jardine
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Local+homotopy+theory"} Local homotopy theory
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4939-2300-7"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4939-2300-7
          %p
            For more see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structure on simplicial presheaves
          %p The local projective model structure on simplicial presheaves appears as theorem 1.6 in
          %ul
            %li
              Benjamin Blander,
              %em Local projective model structure on simplicial presheaves
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.uiuc.edu/K-theory/0462/combination2.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p Its analog for sheaves, theorem 2.1 there, is due to
          %ul
            %li K. Brown, Gersten, …
          %p That the local projective model structure (directly defined) is indeed the left Bousfield localization of the global projective model structure is lemma 4.3 there.
